.TH ORGANIZE-DL 1 "2026-10-23" "organize-dl 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
organize-dl \- sort the files of a directory into category subfolders
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B organize-dl
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIDIRECTORY\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B organize-dl
moves the regular files that sit directly inside
.I DIRECTORY
into subfolders chosen from the file extension.
The default
.I DIRECTORY
is
.IR ~/Downloads .
.PP
Only the top level of
.I DIRECTORY
is read. Hidden files, subdirectories and symbolic links are never
moved. Subfolders are created on demand, so a directory that only holds
images ends up with a single
.I Images
subfolder.
.PP
A file is never overwritten. If the destination name is already taken,
a numeric suffix is inserted before the extension:
.I photo.jpg
becomes
.I photo_1.jpg
and then
.I photo_2.jpg
on the next collision. Compound archive extensions are kept whole, so
.I backup.tar.gz
becomes
.I backup_1.tar.gz
and not
.IR backup.tar_1.gz .
.PP
Files are processed in byte order of their names, which makes a run
reproducible for a given directory content.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Print the planned moves without touching the filesystem.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-device
Print the storage device, mount point, filesystem and free space of
.IR DIRECTORY ,
then exit without moving any file.
.TP
.B \-\-
End of options. Use it when
.I DIRECTORY
starts with a hyphen.
.PP
Options must appear before
.IR DIRECTORY .
.SH CATEGORIES
The extension match is case insensitive and ignores the leading dot.
.TP
.B Images
jpg, jpeg, png, gif, bmp, webp, svg, tif, tiff, heic, avif
.TP
.B Documents
pdf, doc, docx, xls, xlsx, ppt, pptx, txt, md, rtf, odt, ods, odp,
csv, epub
.TP
.B Music
mp3, wav, flac, aac, ogg, m4a, opus, wma
.TP
.B Videos
mp4, mkv, avi, mov, webm, m4v, wmv, flv
.TP
.B Archives
zip, rar, 7z, tar, gz, bz2, xz, tgz, iso
.TP
.B Others
every file that matches none of the above, including files without an
extension
.SH OUTPUT
One line per moved file, in the form
.RI "name " "-> " "Category/name" .
In dry-run mode each line starts with
.IR "[dry-run] " .
A summary line follows:
.RS
.EX
Moved 12 files: Images 5, Documents 4, Music 1, Videos 1, Archives 1.
.EE
.RE
.PP
Only non-empty categories appear in the summary. A dry run prints
.RI "12 files would be moved" " instead."
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every file was moved, or there was nothing to move.
.TP
.B 1
At least one file could not be moved. The remaining files were still
processed.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid option or argument.
.TP
.B 3
.I DIRECTORY
does not exist or is not a directory.
.SH EXAMPLES
Sort the default downloads folder:
.PP
.RS
.EX
organize-dl
.EE
.RE
.PP
Preview what would happen, without moving anything:
.PP
.RS
.EX
organize-dl --dry-run
.EE
.RE
.PP
Show which storage device holds the files, and how much space is left:
.PP
.RS
.EX
organize-dl --device ~/Downloads
.EE
.RE
.PP
Sort another folder, whose name starts with a hyphen:
.PP
.RS
.EX
organize-dl -- -incoming
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mv (1),
.BR mkdir (1)
